            </summary>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
              Slope percentage expresses the steepness of an incline as the vertical rise divided by horizontal run multiplied by 100. For example, a climb of 4 meters over 40 meters of horizontal run produces a slope percentage of (4 / 40) × 100 = 10%.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
