              First, divide the slope percentage by 100 to obtain the decimal slope: m = Slope % / 100. Next, apply the inverse tangent function: Angle θ = arctan(m). For example, for a 25% slope: m = 0.25, and arctan(0.25) ≈ 14.036 degrees.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
