              Take the tangent of the angle in degrees and multiply by 100: Slope % = tan(θ) × 100. For an angle of 30°: tan(30°) ≈ 0.57735, giving a slope percentage of 57.74%.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
