            </summary>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
              Divide the total vertical rise by your target slope percentage and multiply by 100: Run = (Rise × 100) / Target Slope %. For example, to climb a 0.5-meter step using the standard 1:12 ADA guideline (8.333%), you need a horizontal run of (0.5 × 100) / 8.333 ≈ 6.0 meters.
