            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Slope percentage measures vertical rise divided by horizontal run multiplied by 100 ((Rise / Run) × 100). Slope angle is the geometric angle in degrees formed between the inclined surface and the horizontal plane, computed via θ = arctan(Rise / Run). A 100% slope corresponds to a 45-degree angle, not 90 degrees."
