          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can slope percentage be greater than 100%?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. A slope of 100% means the vertical rise equals the horizontal run (a 45° angle). Any slope steeper than 45° has a rise greater than its run, resulting in a slope percentage greater than 100%. For example, a 60° incline has a slope percentage of tan(60°) × 100 ≈ 173.2%."
          }
        },
