          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How is roof pitch calculated in X:12 notation?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "In North American construction, roof pitch is traditionally expressed as X:12, where X represents the inches of vertical rise for every 12 inches of horizontal run. For example, a roof that rises 6 inches over 12 inches of horizontal run has a 6:12 pitch, a slope of 50%, and an inclination angle of approximately 26.57 degrees."
          }
