          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Mathematically, slope is defined on a Cartesian coordinate system as the rate of vertical change with respect to horizontal distance (Δy / Δx). Using the sloped diagonal surface length in the denominator would calculate the sine of the angle rather than the tangent, leading to incorrect slope percentage and pitch calculations."
          }
        }
